---
// Gravel Driveway Structural Crown & Layer Visualizer
---
<section class="section no-print" id="gravel-visualizer">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2>Interactive Driveway Structural Crown & Layer Visualizer</h2>
      <div class="section-divider"></div>
      <p>Inspect the engineered 2% crown profile that sheds stormwater to side swales, dual-layer base compaction, and tire load stress distribution.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="gravel-viz-grid">
      <!-- Driveway Cross-Section with 2% Crown -->
      <div class="gravel-viz-card">
        <div class="card-header">
          <div class="header-title">
            <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8"><rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="2"/><path d="M3 9h18M9 21V9"/></svg>
            <h3>Driveway 2% Crown Cross-Section</h3>
          </div>
          <span class="status-badge green">Stormwater Shedding</span>
        </div>

        <div class="crown-body">
          <div class="crown-diagram-wrap">
            <svg class="crown-svg" viewBox="0 0 400 220" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet">
              <defs>
                <linearGradient id="crusher-base-grad" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1">
                  <stop offset="0%" stop-color="#64748b"/>
                  <stop offset="100%" stop-color="#475569"/>
                </linearGradient>
                <linearGradient id="angular-top-grad" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1">
                  <stop offset="0%" stop-color="#94a3b8"/>
                  <stop offset="100%" stop-color="#64748b"/>
                </linearGradient>
              </defs>

              <!-- Native Subgrade Soil with Side Ditches / Swales -->
              <path d="M 0 120 Q 30 140 60 120 L 340 120 Q 370 140 400 120 L 400 220 L 0 220 Z" fill="#1c1917"/>
              <text x="200" y="200" fill="#78716c" font-size="10" font-weight="600" text-anchor="middle">Compacted Native Subgrade (Excavated Base)</text>

              <!-- Woven Geotextile Stabilization Fabric -->
              <path d="M 60 120 L 340 120" stroke="#f59e0b" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-dasharray="6,3"/>
              <text x="200" y="132" fill="#fbbf24" font-size="8" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">Woven Stabilization Fabric (Prevents Sinking Into Mud)</text>

              <!-- 4" Crusher Run Sub-Base with Crown -->
              <path d="M 60 120 Q 200 100 340 120 L 340 85 Q 200 65 60 85 Z" fill="url(#crusher-base-grad)" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="1"/>
              <text x="200" y="96" fill="#f1f5f9" font-size="9" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">4" - 6" Compacted #411 Crusher Run Base</text>

              <!-- 2" - 3" #57 Clean Angular Top Course with Crown Profile -->
              <path d="M 60 85 Q 200 65 340 85 L 340 60 Q 200 40 60 60 Z" fill="url(#angular-top-grad)" stroke="#475569" stroke-width="1.2"/>
              <text x="200" y="52" fill="#0f172a" font-size="9" font-weight="800" text-anchor="middle">2" - 3" Angular #57 Surface Gravel</text>

              <!-- Crown Height Indicator (Center 2.5" higher than shoulders) -->
              <line x1="200" y1="40" x2="200" y2="60" stroke="#38bdf8" stroke-width="2"/>
              <text x="200" y="32" fill="#38bdf8" font-size="10" font-weight="800" text-anchor="middle">2% Crown (2.5" Center Crest)</text>

              <!-- Water Runoff Arrows to Side Ditches -->
              <path d="M 170 42 Q 120 48 80 65" fill="none" stroke="#38bdf8" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#arrow)"/>
              <path d="M 230 42 Q 280 48 320 65" fill="none" stroke="#38bdf8" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#arrow)"/>
              <text x="70" y="80" fill="#7dd3fc" font-size="8">Runoff to Swale</text>
              <text x="330" y="80" fill="#7dd3fc" font-size="8">Runoff to Swale</text>

              <!-- Vehicle Tire Contact Point -->
              <rect x="130" y="15" width="24" height="30" rx="3" fill="#09090b" stroke="#71717a" stroke-width="2"/>
              <rect x="246" y="15" width="24" height="30" rx="3" fill="#09090b" stroke="#71717a" stroke-width="2"/>
            </svg>
          </div>

          <div class="crown-metrics-grid">
            <div class="c-metric">
              <span class="c-val">2% (1/4" / ft)</span>
              <span class="c-lbl">Slope from Center</span>
            </div>
            <div class="c-metric">
              <span class="c-val">Dual Layer</span>
              <span class="c-lbl">Base + Surface</span>
            </div>
            <div class="c-metric">
              <span class="c-val">Woven Fabric</span>
              <span class="c-lbl">Prevents Mud Pump</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="field-tips-box">
            <div class="tip-title">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z"/><line x1="12" y1="9" x2="12" y2="13"/><line x1="12" y1="17" x2="12.01" y2="17"/></svg>
              The #1 Cause of Driveway Potholes: Standing Water
            </div>
            <p>
              A flat gravel driveway will always develop potholes within one rainy season. Vehicles drive through standing puddles, churning stone and water into slurry that splashes out of the hole. Grading a 2% crown ensures rainwater immediately drains into side swales, keeping your driveway hard and smooth.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Angular Interlock vs Round Gravel Under Tires -->
      <div class="gravel-viz-card">
        <div class="card-header">
          <div class="header-title">
            <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="4"/></svg>
            <h3>Tire Load Stress & Aggregate Interlock</h3>
          </div>
          <span class="status-badge gold">Load Bearing</span>
        </div>

        <div class="interlock-body">
          <div class="interlock-comparison-grid">
            <!-- Angular Crushed Gravel (Locks) -->
            <div class="compare-col good">
              <div class="col-head">Angular #57 Crushed Stone</div>
              <svg class="interlock-svg" viewBox="0 0 160 120">
                <rect width="160" height="120" fill="#090d13" rx="6"/>
                <!-- Heavy Tire on Top -->
                <rect x="50" y="5" width="60" height="25" rx="3" fill="#18181b" stroke="#71717a" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                <!-- Force vectors spreading out diagonally (good!) -->
                <path d="M60 30 L30 100 M100 30 L130 100" stroke="#4ade80" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-dasharray="3,2"/>
                <!-- Interlocking angular polygons -->
                <polygon points="50,45 75,40 80,65 55,70" fill="#94a3b8" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="1"/>
                <polygon points="78,42 105,40 102,68 76,64" fill="#cbd5e1" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="1"/>
                <polygon points="35,68 60,65 65,95 40,90" fill="#64748b" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="1"/>
                <polygon points="62,68 95,65 92,95 65,92" fill="#94a3b8" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="1"/>
                <polygon points="95,65 125,68 120,95 92,92" fill="#cbd5e1" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="1"/>
              </svg>
              <div class="col-verdict ok">
                <strong>Locks Under Tires</strong>
                <span>Angular facets wedge together under vehicle weight, spreading wheel load over large footprint.</span>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Round Pea Gravel (Rutting / Spinning) -->
            <div class="compare-col bad">
              <div class="col-head">Round Pea Gravel (Never Use)</div>
              <svg class="interlock-svg" viewBox="0 0 160 120">
                <rect width="160" height="120" fill="#090d13" rx="6"/>
                <!-- Heavy Tire Sunk Down -->
                <rect x="50" y="25" width="60" height="25" rx="3" fill="#18181b" stroke="#ef4444" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                <!-- Rutting arrows pushing stones out to sides -->
                <path d="M48 45 L15 45 M112 45 L145 45" stroke="#ef4444" stroke-width="2.5"/>
                <!-- Spherical stones rolling out -->
                <circle cx="35" cy="45" r="10" fill="#f59e0b"/>
                <circle cx="125" cy="45" r="10" fill="#f59e0b"/>
                <circle cx="50" cy="75" r="11" fill="#d97706"/>
                <circle cx="75" cy="75" r="12" fill="#f59e0b"/>
                <circle cx="100" cy="75" r="11" fill="#d97706"/>
                <circle cx="60" cy="98" r="11" fill="#b45309"/>
                <circle cx="85" cy="98" r="11" fill="#f59e0b"/>
              </svg>
              <div class="col-verdict warn">
                <strong>Causes Rutting & Tire Spin</strong>
                <span>Round stones act like marbles under wheels, displacing sideways and sinking vehicle tires.</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="field-tips-box">
            <div class="tip-title">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12" y2="12"/><line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12.01" y2="16"/></svg>
              Driveway Geotextile: Woven vs Non-Woven
            </div>
            <p>
              Always specify <strong>woven stabilization fabric</strong> (such as Mirafi 500X) beneath driveway rock, not light non-woven garden weed barrier. Woven fabric has high tensile strength (CBR puncture resistance > 800 lbs), bridging soft spots in clay soils and preventing driveway gravel from sinking into the subsoil.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
.gravel-viz-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1.15fr 1fr;
  gap: var(--space-6);
  margin-top: var(--space-4);
}

@media (max-width: 900px) {
  .gravel-viz-grid {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }
}

.gravel-viz-card {
  background: var(--surface-raised);
  border: 1px solid var(--surface-glass-border);
  border-radius: var(--radius-xl);
  overflow: hidden;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
}

.card-header {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-5);
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--surface-glass-border);
  background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.02);
}

.header-title {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: var(--space-2);
}

.header-title svg {
  color: var(--gold-400);
}

.header-title h3 {
  font-size: 0.95rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  margin: 0;
}

.crown-body, .interlock-body {
  padding: var(--space-5);
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: var(--space-4);
}

.crown-diagram-wrap {
  background: #090d13;
  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  padding: var(--space-3);
  border: 1px solid var(--surface-glass-border);
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center;
}

.crown-svg {
  width: 100%;
  max-width: 400px;
  height: auto;
}

.crown-metrics-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
  gap: var(--space-3);
}

.c-metric {
  background: var(--surface-card);
  padding: var(--space-3);
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  text-align: center;
  border: 1px solid var(--surface-glass-border);
}

.c-val {
  display: block;
  font-size: 1.05rem;
  font-weight: 800;
  color: var(--gold-400);
}

.c-lbl {
  font-size: 0.7rem;
  color: var(--text-secondary);
}

.interlock-comparison-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
  gap: var(--space-3);
}

@media (max-width: 500px) {
  .interlock-comparison-grid {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }
}

.compare-col {
  background: var(--surface-card);
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  padding: var(--space-3);
  border: 1px solid var(--surface-glass-border);
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: var(--space-2);
}

.compare-col.good {
  border-color: rgba(74, 222, 128, 0.3);
}

.compare-col.bad {
  border-color: rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.3);
}

.col-head {
  font-size: 0.78rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  color: var(--text-primary);
  text-align: center;
}

.interlock-svg {
  width: 100%;
  height: auto;
}

.col-verdict {
  font-size: 0.72rem;
  line-height: 1.4;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 2px;
}

.col-verdict.ok strong {
  color: #4ade80;
}

.col-verdict.warn strong {
  color: #ef4444;
}

.col-verdict span {
  color: var(--text-secondary);
}

.status-badge {
  font-size: 0.7rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  padding: 3px 10px;
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
}

.status-badge.green {
  background: rgba(74, 222, 128, 0.12);
  color: #4ade80;
  border: 1px solid rgba(74, 222, 128, 0.3);
}

.status-badge.gold {
  background: rgba(234, 179, 8, 0.12);
  color: #fbbf24;
  border: 1px solid rgba(234, 179, 8, 0.3);
}

.field-tips-box {
  background: rgba(234, 179, 8, 0.08);
  border: 1px solid rgba(234, 179, 8, 0.25);
  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  padding: var(--space-4);
}

.tip-title {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: var(--space-2);
  color: #fbbf24;
  font-size: 0.8rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
}

.field-tips-box p {
  font-size: 0.78rem;
  line-height: 1.55;
  color: var(--text-secondary);
  margin: 0;
}
</style>
